    {
      "id": "062e6645-6887-ef11-8474-000d3a37e3b6",
      "type": "GeneralText",
      "area": "General",
      "position": 1,
      "content": "Articulation Agreement Overview This agreement outlines lower-division course requirements specific to the major. Students are strongly encouraged to consult an academic advisor to ensure they meet all degree requirements for their intended baccalaureate program. Helpful Resources: CSUB Catalog Transfer Admission Requirements Academic Advising Student Centers CSUB Program Pathways Mapper Course Equivalency Information for 4-Year Institutions Students and staff can explore course transfer equivalencies through the Transfer Evaluation System (TES) . Equivalency agreements are updated regularly and subject to change. For the most current information, please refer to TES or contact the Articulation Office .",
      "contentHtml": "<p><strong>Articulation Agreement Overview</strong></p><p>This agreement outlines lower-division course requirements specific to the major. Students are strongly encouraged to consult an academic advisor to ensure they meet all degree requirements for their intended baccalaureate program.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Helpful Resources:</strong></p><ul><li><a href=\"https://catalog.csub.edu/\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">CSUB Catalog</a></li><li><a href=\"https://www.csub.edu/admissions/transfer\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Transfer Admission Requirements</a></li><li><a href=\"https://www.csub.edu/advising\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Academic Advising Student Centers</a></li><li><a href=\"https://www.csub.edu/ppm\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">CSUB Program Pathways Mapper</a></li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong>Course Equivalency Information for 4-Year Institutions</strong></p><p>Students and staff can explore course transfer equivalencies through the <a href=\"https://tes.collegesource.com/publicview/TES_publicview01.aspx?rid=7ea49506-39bf-4815-8199-734369e7a30c&amp;aid=ccc830a2-2435-4dd6-b352-a586b4575654\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Transfer Evaluation System (TES)</a>. Equivalency agreements are updated regularly and subject to change. For the most current information, please refer to TES or contact the <a href=\"https://www.csub.edu/articulation/\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Articulation Office</a>.</p>"
    },
    {
      "id": "082e6645-6887-ef11-8474-000d3a37e3b6",
      "type": "GeneralTitle",
      "area": "General",
      "position": 2,
      "content": "About the Major",
      "contentHtml": null
    },
    {
      "id": "092e6645-6887-ef11-8474-000d3a37e3b6",
      "type": "GeneralText",
      "area": "General",
      "position": 3,
      "content": "The Interdisciplinary Studies Programs at CSUB allow students to examine concepts, issues, and perspectives that cross traditional boundaries of study, and to combine elements of distinct disciplines uniquely. For more information, visit the following: Department of Interdisciplinary Studies Program Requirements - Interdisciplinary Studies, BA, Women, Gender, and Sexuality Studies Concentration",
      "contentHtml": "<p><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">The Interdisciplinary Studies Programs at CSUB allow students to examine concepts, issues, and perspectives that cross traditional boundaries of study, and to combine elements of distinct disciplines uniquely.</span></p><p><br></p><p>For more information, visit the following:</p><p>Department of <a href=\"https://www.csub.edu/academicprograms/interdisciplinary-programs\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Interdisciplinary Studies</a></p><p>Program Requirements - <a href=\"https://catalog.csub.edu/academic-degrees-programs/undergraduate-majors/interdisciplinary-studies-ba-women-gender-sexuality-studies-concentration/#programrequirementstext\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Interdisciplinary Studies, BA, Women, Gender, and Sexuality Studies Concentration</a></p>"
    }
